%% C4 Dynamic diagram: the office fire, times as measured in Section 11
sequenceDiagram
  participant SRC as Source and physics
  participant SEN as Sensors
  participant INT as Intelligence
  participant ACT as Interlocks and actuation
  participant EVA as Evacuation
  participant BS as BuildSim
  SRC->>SEN: 1: fire lit at t=0.<br/>Smoke, CO and heat<br/>rise every step
  SEN->>INT: 2: a reading every 5 s,<br/>lagged, noisy, clamped
  Note over INT: 3: t=51 s, P reaches 0.35: INVESTIGATING
  Note over INT: 4: t=81 s, P above 0.55 for 20 s: PRE-ALARM
  Note over INT: 5: t=106 s, 25 s in pre-alarm, P=0.91: CONFIRMED
  INT->>ACT: 6: sprinkler on, door closed,<br/>evacuate, each with its reason
  ACT->>SRC: 7: allowed. 331 °C corroborates the smoke, the room is empty and off-route.<br/>Sprinkler on and door openness 0.15 are written into the world
  ACT->>EVA: 8: everyone in the building<br/>starts evacuating
  EVA->>BS: 9: the route out of the fire room,<br/>41 nodes down to exit A1016
  SRC->>SEN: 10: next step, heat x0.25<br/>and smoke x0.4.<br/>The readings bend
  SRC->>BS: 11: once a simulated second: heat maps, effects, alerts, doors, people, sensor labels
  EVA->>BS: 12: t=217 s, last person out.<br/>RSET recorded
